<!--
  ============================================================================
  INTERLOCK RAT — Wazuh Active Response (v2)
  Author: Makhan Singh — Seneca Polytechnic, SPR600 Security Monitoring
  File:   /var/ossec/etc/ossec.conf  (append inside <ossec_config>)

  This snippet PRESERVES the original active-response configuration from the
  lab manual §11.2 — firing firewall-drop on rule 100001 (PowerShell Bypass)
  and rule 100003 (Registry Run key persistence) for 600 seconds — so that
  the existing report and Wazuh active-response screenshots remain accurate.

  Restart manager after edits: sudo systemctl restart wazuh-manager
  ============================================================================
-->
<active-response>
  <command>firewall-drop</command>
  <location>local</location>
  <rules_id>100001,100003</rules_id>
  <timeout>600</timeout>
</active-response>

<!--
  ============================================================================
  OPTIONAL UPGRADE PATH (commented out — uncomment to replace the block above)
  ============================================================================
  Production SOC best-practice would auto-block only on the highest-confidence
  detections, since rule 100001 alone (PowerShell -ep Bypass) has a moderate
  false-positive rate against legitimate sysadmin workflows.

  The block below auto-contains on:
    100007  PowerShell hidden + bypass chained (universal dropper signature)
    100008  Encoded PowerShell with base64 (rare in benign use)
    100013  IFEO Debugger registry write (almost always malicious)
    100017  DNS query for *.trycloudflare.com (real-world Interlock C2 IOC)
    100020  Defender service stop/disable attempt
    100025  Correlated encoded-PS + outbound network within 60s (level 15)

  Rules 100001 and 100003 still alert at level 12/14 but no longer auto-block,
  preserving the kill-chain for IR investigation.

  <active-response>
    <command>firewall-drop</command>
    <location>local</location>
    <rules_id>100007,100008,100013,100017,100020,100025</rules_id>
    <timeout>600</timeout>
  </active-response>
-->
